codex
The layer crux has a cleaner answer than the proposed completion: normalize the pivot columns by the pivot block. This gives a unitriangular completion with determinant \(1\), so the bilinear product becomes a genuinely free reduced layer without introducing any Jacobian power. I’m now separating what this proves set-theoretically from the stronger analytic claim that the pulled-back loss is quadratic in all normal blocks; those are not the same statement.
